    def gnb_xn_handover_preparation_param(self, **kwargs):
        """
        :param id: Local identifier for gNodeB
        :param max_repetitions: (Optional) Maximum number of times RAN will send Xn Handover Request when failed
        :param bwp_id_ulFullPwrTx: (Optional) bwp_id:ul_FullPowerTransmission_r16
        :param action: (Optional) Specifies what action will be done when the nth occurence is met
        :param hex: (Optional) Value of hex payload to send for override_resp an
               d send_hex_then_respond (if available) action
        :param nth: (Optional) Specifies which occurrence of the procedure should the specified action be performed
        :param ntimes: (Optional) Specifies the number of times the specified action should be performed
        :param time_to_wait: (Optional) Specifies the time delay in seconds whenever action is equivalent to delay.
        :param cause: (Optional) Sets cause value for NG-RAN Configuration Update Failure or Error Indication
        :param msg: (Optional) Specifies which message of the procedure should the specified action be performed.
        :param errortype: (Optional) Specifies error type for a particular reactionType
        :param criticality: (Optional) Specifies Type of Criticality for Abstract_Syntax_Error
        :param procedure: (Optional) Specifies the procedure that should be conc
               urrently executed with the procedure associated with this command
        :param overheatingAssistanceConfig: (Optional) setup or release overheat
               ingAssistanceConfig in HO Request message for both Xn and NG HO when RANSIM is ac
               ting as source
        :param ue_sec_algos_first_bit_reserved_xn: (Optional) Toggle the mode in
                which Security algorithms in UE Security Capabilities IE in Xn Handover Request/
               Acknowledge message will be encoded/decoded. If set to 'on' then first bit (bit-0
               ) is taken as reserved and algorithms will be considered from second bit (bit-1)
               onwards. If set to 'off' then algorithms will be considered from first bit (bit-0
               ) onwards and fourth bit (bit-3) onwards is reserved. System default settings sha
               ll be Off'. When the Xn peer is a real gnb, this parameter should be set in sync
               with actXnSecCapNewMode parameter of that gnb
        :param ReleasePreferenceConfig: (Optional) setup or release ReleasePrefe
               renceConfig in HO Request message for both Xn and NG HO when RANSIM is acting as
               source
        :param drb_qos_map_modification: (Optional) Applicable when action=modify_drb_qos_mapping
        :param unsupported_extension_type: (Optional) Applicable when action=add
               _unsupported_extensions to introduce unupported extension types.
        :param pdu_sessions: (Optional) Applicable only when action=drb_qos_map_
               modification, to specify the PDU session ids in which the DRB-QOS mappingshould b
               e manipulated
        :param reestab_info: (Optional) Cell id to be included in Reestablishmen
               tInfo in handover request message and a flag that indicates whether the shortmac
               for that cell id should be valid or invalid. This param is applicable only for In
               tra5gs HO.
        :param reestab_ncell_info: (Optional) List of Cell ids to be included in
                reestablish Ncell info and a flag for each cell id, that indicates whether the s
               hortmac for that cell id should be valid or invalid. This param is applicable onl
               y for Intra5gs HO.
        :param include_masked_imeisv: (Optional) When set to on, the Masked IMEI
               SV IE is included in the Xn Handover Request
        :param include_sidelink: (Optional) Include sidelink IE in handover preparation information.
        :param sidelink_value: (Optional) Specifies the value to be used for the
                sidelink information element. This is optional and if this value is not provided
               , FFFFFFFF value will be encoded internally
        :param exclude_dataforwardinginfofromSource: (Optional) exclude dataforw
               ardinginfofromSource IE in handover preparation information
        :param include_security_config: (Optional) Set to enable, to include 'se
               curity algorithm configuration' Information element in Handover preparation infor
               mation.
        :param sec_config_nea: (Optional) Encrytion algorithm (nea) to be sent i
               n security algorithm configuration' Information element, if include_security_conf
               ig is set to 'enable'
        :param sec_config_nia: (Optional) Integrity algorithm (nia) to be sent i
               n security algorithm configuration' Information element, if include_security_conf
               ig is set to 'enable'
        :param mobility_information: (Optional) Bit index 0(LSB bit) , if set to
                value: 0 - Indicates RSRP threshold was used to trigger Handover 1 - Indicates R
               SRQ threshold was used to trigger Handover
        """

        self._wtsemu_egate_controller.egate_command_executor(
            "gnb_xn_handover_preparation_param", **kwargs
        )

