    def cqi_algo_control_ota_testmode_nr(self, **kwargs):
        """
        :param profile_id: Test profile id
        :param delete: (Optional) delete the test profile,Options : yes|no; true
               |false; 1|0 ; on|off and Set it to true|yes|on|1 to delete the profile.
        :param cqi_obs_period: (Optional) It defines the time between two CQI Re
               porting Interval. In this duration work related to RULE 2 will be executed.This i
               s the smallest unit which will be used in the egate command. (Parameter in egate
               command)The minimum value of this parameter can be 1.The CQI Observation period c
               an be changed to CSI-Measurement Period
        :param cqi_reporting_window: (Optional) This multiplier N can have minim
               um value of 1 ( Based on Observation Period & Observation Period Type sepcified).
               This value N determines when CQI in the CSI Report gets updated (if required).If
               N&gt; 1 lets say N=3 and CQI Observation Period = 1, it means the Updation of the
                CQI value in the CSI Report will only occur (if needed) Once in 3 Reporting Inte
               rval or as aligned with Observation Period Type.
        :param nack_reference_level: (Optional) This parameter control the absol
               ute level of HARQ nacks which should sustainable by the system.
        :param logging_choice: (Optional) Logging Type will have modes as below:
               CHOICE_NONE     - DefaultAPP_ONLY      - App Logs (syslogs/l2sm logs)EGATE_ONLY
                 - Only Egate consoleBOTH_CHOICES     - Both App and Egate console
        :param log_interval: (Optional) This parameter controls at what interval
               s of time , logging of Internal state of CQI determination algo parameters needs
               to be dumped in the Log (syslog/L2SM logs).Printing in the egate console can also
                be triggered or made configurableValue should be taken as multiples of CQI Repor
               ting Interval.Default value can be 0 (which mean no logging)If logging type is NO
               T Null , log_interval cannot be zero
        :param cqi_average: (Optional) Number of values used to calculate the Average BLER to update CQI value.
        :param qam_to_cqi_range: (Optional) This parameter controls the mapping of QAM to CQI values.
        :param choice_algo_or_init_cqi: (Optional) This parameter controls the c
               hoice of CQI algorithm or initial CQI value.MIN - Minimum value for CQI algorithm
                or initial CQI valueMAX - Maximum value for CQI algorithm or initial CQI value
        :param smoothing_on: (Optional) This parameter controls the smoothing of
                CQI values. If set to true, CQI values will be smoothed over time. If set to fal
               se, CQI values will be taken as is.
        :param report_immediately: (Optional) This parameter controls whether CQ
               I values should be reported immediately or not. If set to true, CQI values will b
               e reported immediately. If set to false, CQI values will be reported at the next
               reporting interval.
        """

        self._wtsemu_egate_controller.egate_command_executor(
            "cqi_algo_control_ota_testmode_nr", **kwargs
        )

